// The aborting write door is kept, and still aborts. `Process.write` to a child that is gone is
// `E0021` — "fatal by default, recoverable when you ask" is the language's established shape, and
// removing the aborting half would break every program that legitimately treats a dead child as
// the end of the run. The recoverable half is `try_write` (see os_try_write.noe), which reports
// the identical message as a value.
// expect: error E0021 at 11:1
// expect: exit 1
use std.{os}

gone = os.spawn("dead", [])
gone.write("input")
echo "unreached"
